{"agent":"fleet-ciagentenv","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":2,"detail":"The added autouse fixture calls `monkeypatch.delenv(\"DDFLOW_AGENT\", raising=False)` before every test, so every `run_cli` subprocess in this file is spawned from an environment that no longer contains `DDFLOW_AGENT` regardless of what the gate runner does. Consequently this suite behaves identically on the unfixed `runner.py` (`**os.environ`) and the fixed one (`**child_env(...)`): the three `clone_id_recovery` tests pass in both cases, so this is not a regression test for the change — it only neutralizes the trigger. Given \"with `DDFLOW_AGENT` exported\" (the exact precondition the bug describes) the new fixture removes it in-process, so the reproducer cannot be observed and the actual fix (scrubbing `DDFLOW_AGENT`/`DDFLOW_SESSION_ID` inside the gate's child env) is left uncovered; a future removal of the `child_env` call would not be caught by any test. The regression test should instead export the variable and assert that the command gate’s child environment no longer carries it (and would fail on the pre-fix runner), rather than deleting it in the test process [D-rules-hierarchy].","digest":"a4a4bbb1cb847f26","location":"tests/test_clone_id_recovery.py:55 (`_no_caller_identity` fixture)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_clone_id_recovery.py:55 (`_no_caller_identity` fixture)"}],"chunks_total":3,"coverage":"3/3 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":11512,"diff_sha":"8d1a8a818fab413011ef44a6742828f9643d42c55addd065785aea16d6a0bff8","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":259.3,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"8f13c15978a089ac","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/fix-B3a8e04ca38.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261015T20